<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 11.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 11.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended January 11:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   255	   0.98     373250  95.18    20.04</p>
<p>Reliance	     220	   0.86     334900  73.68    20.38</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   186	   0.71     379750  70.63    19.90</p>
<p>ITC		    345	   0.80     118400  40.85    12.09</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    355	   1.33     114950  40.81    19.54</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    245	   0.21     108500  26.58     4.47</p>
<p>Tata Power	   133	   0.52     169200  22.50    20.39</p>
<p>BSES		   220	   0.23	82800  18.22     5.45</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 136	   0.52     112300  15.27    19.94</p>
<p>Sterlite	     245	   0.95	49900  12.23    20.22</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 17.84 percent on an annualised basis against 16.15 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Jan 4.</p>
